				<article id="post-1537" class="entry content-bg single-entry post-1537 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-kitchen-pantry-hacks category-small-space-decor">
	<div class="entry-content-wrap">
		
<div class="entry-content single-content">
	
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">The best over kitchen cabinet decorating ideas turn that awkward gap between the cabinets and the ceiling into a finishing touch instead of a dust-collecting jumble. Done well, a few baskets, crocks or plants up there make a kitchen look taller, warmer and more finished. Done badly, it looks like overflow storage.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This guide shows you how to match the decor to the size of the gap, a simple 6-step method and 14 ideas, from woven baskets and stoneware to hidden LED lights and seasonal touches. You will also find what to keep away from the range and how to stay safe when you climb up to style or dust.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image size-full"><img fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" width="1024" height="1024" src="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/above-kitchen-cabinet-decor-01-sage-kitchen.jpg" alt="Over kitchen cabinet decorating ideas: sage green upper cabinets topped with woven baskets, two stoneware jugs and a trailing pothos plant, above an oak open shelf with plates and a counter with a sink, brass faucet and a dining table in front" class="wp-image-1529" srcset="https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/above-kitchen-cabinet-decor-01-sage-kitchen.jpg 1024w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/above-kitchen-cabinet-decor-01-sage-kitchen-300x300.jpg 300w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/above-kitchen-cabinet-decor-01-sage-kitchen-150x150.jpg 150w, https://dailyspacehacks.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/above-kitchen-cabinet-decor-01-sage-kitchen-768x768.jpg 768w" sizes="(max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px" /></figure>



<div class="wp-block-group dsh-summary has-background" style="border-radius:12px;border-left-color:#8FA689;border-left-width:5px;background-color:#EEF3EC;padding-top:20px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:20px;padding-left:24px"><div class="wp-block-group__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-container-core-group-is-layout-0d2d72cd wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Key Takeaways</strong></p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Quick answer:</strong> To decorate above kitchen cabinets, measure the gap to the ceiling, choose a few large pieces that fit it, such as woven baskets, stoneware crocks, faux trailing greenery or leaning art, arrange them in two or three spaced groups and keep the area near the range hood clear.</li>



<li>Fewer, bigger pieces look better than many small ones, which read as clutter from the floor.</li>



<li>Use a sturdy step stool with a handrail, never a chair, when you style or dust up high.</li>
</ul>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Time:</strong> 1–2 hours · <strong>Cost:</strong> $0–120 · <strong>Difficulty:</strong> Easy</p>
</div></div>


